  "notes": [
    "Small landscape card, foliation 7, headed Thm 1. It defines h_X from homotopy classes of maps to principal-covering classes and states equivalence between universal classification and contractibility of E. The definition uses de X, the label df, and the symbol ∀ in condition 1. The theorem is transcribed as stated; its unrestricted phrase tout espace is not silently narrowed, and no proof check of that generality is claimed.",
    "Blue tout lies in the gap on the line. Blue bi replaces an uncertain dark prefix before jectif. The isolated blue sign below H^1 is drawn literally, with no assigned numeral. The heavily retraced B and the beginning of princi-paux are kept without inventing cancelled letters. No date."
  ],
  "hand": [
    "On this card the black writing compresses entire syllables to a low continuous stroke; dots or accents remain isolated above them. Blue revisions can lie directly over black letters: bijectif is the clearest example, leaving the old prefix doubtful. The reinforced B here still has two distinct bowls. H expands df and the ∀ symbol and changes de X to sur X; C misplaces the isolated blue sign in a margin."
  ],
